  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIowa County, Iowa - County Government and Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n Menu\n \n \n\n \n\n About \n \n\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n Elected Officials\n School Districts\n Township Officials\n \n \n \n\n Departments \n \n\n 911\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Conservation\n Emergency Management\n Emergency Medical Services\n Engineer\n Environmental Health\n General Relief\n Medical Examiner\n Mental Health\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Transportation\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n Zoning\n All Departments\n \n \n \n\n Supervisors \n \n\n Boards & Commissions\n County Ordinances\n Fireworks Permits \n Meetings & Minutes\n Policies\n \n \n Contact\n \n \n\n Clear · 43°\n Calendar\n Courts\n Elections\n Employment\n FAQ\n \n\n Translate Language\n \n Translate\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to\n Iowa County, Iowa\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Board Meetings \n \n \n\n \n \n Elections & Voting \n \n \n\n \n \n Property & Tax Info \n \n \n\n \n \n Real Estate Inquiry \n \n \n\n \n \n Renew Vehicle Tags \n \n \n\n \n \n Vital Records \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \nThings to Know\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n\n Auditor\n Absentee Ballots\n Posted October 15, 2026\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n\n Employment\n 2 Job Openings\n Posted October 12, 2026\n \n \n \n \n\n \nAll NewsEmploymentBid Notices\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \nStream Supervisor Meetings\n \nStay connected with Iowa County by subscribing to our new YouTube channel, where you can watch live and archived Board of Supervisor Meetings. \n \n \n\n YouTube Channel\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Events\n View Full Calendar\n\n\n\n \n\n \nOctober 21\n \n\n Homeschool Discovery Days - Whooo Ate That? – Owl Investigation\n 10:00 am\n 2550 G Ave\n\n \nLadora, IA \n \n\n \nHomeschool Discovery Days - Whooo Ate That? – Owl Investigation\n 2550 G Ave\n Ladora, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 21, 2026 \n 10:00 am · 11:00am \n\nDiscover the amazing world of owls! We’ll learn about the special adaptations that help owls hunt at night and put our own listening skills to the test with a fun owl hunting activity. Then, become a wildlife detective as we dissect real owl pellets! Participants will carefully uncover and identify tiny bones to discover what an owl has been eating and learn more about the important role owls play in the food chain. This hands-on program is designed for homeschool families of all ages. Come ready to listen, investigate, and discover the fascinating world of owls! Registration is required. Please sign up online at this link Homeschool-Discovery-Days-Whooo-Ate-That-Owl-Investigation sign-up . Only students need to register for this program. Please dress for the weather, as part of the program will take place outdoors. \n \n\nAre you part of a larger private homeschool group? Contact us to learn about scheduling a separate Homeschool Discovery Day for your group! For More Information\n \nContact: Molly Minnich \n(319) 655-8465 \nmhicks@iowacounty.iowa.gov \nWebsite \n\n Posted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \nNovember 14\n \n\n Open Nature Center Saturday\n 10:00 am\n \n \n\n \nOpen Nature Center Saturday\n Ladora, IA\n \n\n November 14, 2026 \n 10:00 am · 2:00pm \n\nake Iowa Nature Center (LINC) will be open for visitors one Saturday a month 10a-2p from September 2026 through April 2027. LINC will be open for you to explore inside, do some fun interactive activities, and learn about nature. Each Saturday will have a program, see topics, dates, and times below. \n \n\nSeptember 5th - Monarchs anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nOctober 10th - Leaf Crafts anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nNovember 14th - Wild Turkeys 1-2p \n \n\nDecember 5th - Holiday Nature Crafts anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nJanurary 9th - Animals in the Winter 1-2p \n \n\nFeburary 6th - Snowshoeing and Snow Art anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nMarch 6th - Pinecone Bird Feeder anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nApril 3rd - Learn to Fish anytime 10a-2p For More Information\n \nContact: Mary Blair \n(319) 655-8466 \nmblair@iowacounty.iowa.gov \nWebsite \n\n Posted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \nNovember 18\n \n\n Homeschool Discovery Days - Hidden Colors of Fall – Leaf Chromatograph\n 10:00 am\n 2550 G Ave\n\n \nLadora, IA \n \n\n \nHomeschool Discovery Days - Hidden Colors of Fall – Leaf Chromatograph\n 2550 G Ave\n Ladora, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n November 18, 2026 \n 10:00 am · 11:00am \n\nHave you ever wondered why leaves change color in the fall? Become a nature scientist as we uncover the hidden colors inside autumn leaves! Participants will use leaf chromatography to separate the different pigments found in leaves and discover that there may be more colors hiding inside a leaf than we can see. After our experiment, we’ll head outdoors to explore the trees around us. We’ll investigate fallen leaves, look for differences between tree species, and discover what happens to deciduous trees as they prepare for winter.  Registration is required. Please sign up online at this link Homeschool-Discovery-Days-Hidden-Colors-of-Fall-Leaf-Chromatograph sign-up  Only students need to register for this program.  Please dress for the weather, as part of the program will take place outdoors. \n \n\nAre you part of a larger private homeschool group? Contact us to learn about scheduling a separate Homeschool Discovery Day for your group! For More Information\n \nContact: Molly Minnich \n(319) 655-8465 \nmhicks@iowacounty.iowa.gov \nWebsite \n\n Posted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \nDecember 5\n \n\n Open Nature Center Saturday\n 10:00 am\n \n \n\n \nOpen Nature Center Saturday\n Ladora, IA\n \n\n December 5, 2026 \n 10:00 am · 2:00pm \n\nake Iowa Nature Center (LINC) will be open for visitors one Saturday a month 10a-2p from September 2026 through April 2027. LINC will be open for you to explore inside, do some fun interactive activities, and learn about nature. Each Saturday will have a program, see topics, dates, and times below. \n \n\nSeptember 5th - Monarchs anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nOctober 10th - Leaf Crafts anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nNovember 14th - Wild Turkeys 1-2p \n \n\nDecember 5th - Holiday Nature Crafts anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nJanurary 9th - Animals in the Winter 1-2p \n \n\nFeburary 6th - Snowshoeing and Snow Art anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nMarch 6th - Pinecone Bird Feeder anytime 10a-2p \n \n\nApril 3rd - Learn to Fish anytime 10a-2p For More Information\n \nContact: Mary Blair \n(319) 655-8466 \nmblair@iowacounty.iowa.gov \nWebsite \n\n Posted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nAbout Iowa County \n \n\nIowa County, Iowa, was established in 1843. It is home to 7 communities, the Amana Colonies, and over 16,000 residents. The County is administered by a five-member Board of Supervisors who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n County Courthouse\n \n901 Court Avenue\n\n Marengo, Iowa 52301\n\n Iowa County East Annex\n \n970 Court Avenue\n\n Marengo, Iowa 52301\n\n \n \n\n\n Hours\n \nMonday - Friday\n\n 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n\n \nClosed Holidays\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Iowa County | Title VI Information\n \npowered by \n \n\n\n\n\n \nTitle VI Information\n \n \nAssurances\n \nNondiscrimination Policy Statement\n \nResolution\n \n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeteran's Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\n \nDay After Thanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\n \n\n\n"
}
